{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their own.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"title":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","externalID":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro"},{"type":"text","text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s library declares the macro and the same kind for reading. It re-exports LinkerSets,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because the expansion names LinkerSets’ types in its users’ files:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    public static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its users then register and find routes:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes the same record "},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes, in the same section, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute ("},{"code":"'@Route' applies to static members only","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Each kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it."}]},{"anchor":"Registering-types","level":3,"text":"Registering types","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro attached to a struct, enum, class or actor stores the type’s metatype. To read the types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a protocol they share, without casting, the plugin names that protocol in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record then holds ","type":"text"},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", read with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A type that doesn’t conform fails to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile where it’s declared: “cannot convert value of type ‘NotAnEvent.Type’ to type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘any AnalyticsEvent.Type’”. Qualify the protocol with its module so a type of the same name at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the use site can’t stand in for it. Without a required protocol, a type’s record holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Any.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registered type can be nested in another from swift-syntax 600 on. Before 600 a macro can’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see where its declaration sits, so the type must be declared at file scope."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Writing-the-expansion-yourself","level":3,"text":"Writing the expansion yourself","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" supplies the peer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expansion"},{"text":". A macro that needs more writes its own and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calls ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" from it for the record. That’s how","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a macro adds the conformance as well, so its users write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event struct Login {}"},{"text":" without naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the protocol. The macro takes an extension role beside the peer:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro, ExtensionMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","","    \/\/ The record, as a peer.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","    }","","    \/\/ The conformance the record requires, as an extension.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        attachedTo declaration: some DeclGroupSyntax,","        providingExtensionsOf type: some TypeSyntaxProtocol,","        conformingTo protocols: [TypeSyntax],","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [ExtensionDeclSyntax] {","        [try ExtensionDeclSyntax(\"extension \\(type.trimmed): Events.AnalyticsEvent {}\")]","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro with both roles:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@attached(peer)","@attached(extension, conformances: AnalyticsEvent)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"EventsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A type can then carry data of its own through the protocol (a schema, a name) while the record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds only its metatype, read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Skipping-a-record-instead-of-refusing-it","level":3,"text":"Skipping a record instead of refusing it","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The expansion refuses what a record can’t hold with an error. A macro that would rather skip some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of those (a generic event that its library lists by hand, say) asks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" first. It returns a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","type":"reference"},{"text":" whose ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/reason-swift.property","type":"reference"},{"text":" says why, and whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/node","type":"reference"},{"text":" is where to report it, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the declaration can hold a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public static func expansion(","    of node: AttributeSyntax,","    providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","    in context: some MacroExpansionContext",") throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","    if let refusal = try refusal(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context),","       refusal.reason == .genericType {","        context.diagnose(Diagnostic(node: refusal.node, message: GenericEventNote()))","        return []","    }","    return try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other refusal still reaches "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws it. Where a declaration sits (in a function’s body, a protocol or a generic type) is seen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from swift-syntax 600 on; before it those three aren’t returned, and the compiler refuses them in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the expansion."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"],"title":"Declaring a macro","anchor":"Declaring-a-macro"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"],"title":"Diagnostics","anchor":"Diagnostics"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport"},"references":{"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacrodiagnostic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why a linker-set macro refuses a declaration or a kind, with the message the compiler shows,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"naming the macro as it was written ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":"), and the node the message points at."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","role":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic/node":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The node the message points at: the declaration, or the attribute for a kind."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"node"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax0B0V","text":"Syntax"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacrodiagnostic\/node","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/node","type":"topic","title":"node","role":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic/reason-swift.property":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacrodiagnost